koupinator/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chkoupinator/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-16T22:51:29Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T22:52:50Z","body":"> it is likely that there will be many problems only discovered after merging, so this PR would need to be merged very early in a release cycle, such as before the first dev release of 4.7.\r\n\r\nfully agreed with you @aaronfranke, so this would be the right time for it to be merged right?\r\n\r\nI really hope this can go through, I will reiterate this: \r\n\r\nGiven that serializing resources to usr:// is a bad idea, JSON is one of the best alternatives to save data. However when trying to store a resource UID as an int it will show up correctly in the JSON file but then be read incorrectly which can be a very frustrating bug to figure out (I had to deal with it myself).\r\n\r\nThe solution of using id_to_text when writing then text_to_id when reading is a very annoying solution (especially when a resource UID is nested deep within a dict) I really wish it was not necessary...","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4263958173/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comm